  "_comment": "Canonical technology allowlist for the `technologies:` frontmatter field on chapter files. Adding a technology here does not add it to any chapter; chapters declare coverage explicitly in their own frontmatter. Inclusion rule for a chapter to list a technology: the chapter must either (a) devote ~500+ words (roughly a full subsection) to it, or (b) use it as the primary chosen example in a major comparison, trade-off, or worked case study. Passing mentions (`unlike Kafka`, `Redis also has this`) do not qualify. This list and the `categories` map below are consumed by scripts/check-frontmatter.mjs (validation) and site/generate.py (the /technologies/ index page). When adding a new technology: include it in `allowed`, assign it to a category, and pick a canonical capitalisation that matches the vendor's own writing (e.g. PostgreSQL not postgres, Cassandra not cassandra). Aliases like `Postgres` and `WebSocket` (singular) should NOT be added; authors should use the canonical form.",
